  "query_preview": "(Friday night through Tuesday)...\nA second low pressure system to the north will move quickly into \nCalifornia for Friday night and Saturday. Showers will increase \nfor Friday night into Saturday morning, then decrease Saturday \nafternoon. Additional rainfall from Friday night through Saturday \nafternoon could range from around 0.50 near the coast to 0.50 to 1\ninch on the coastal slopes of the mountains. That system for \nSaturday could also bring stronger winds to the coastal waters for\nFriday night and for the mountains and deserts for late Friday \nnight through Saturday.\n\nSaturday night through Sunday afternoon should be relatively \ndrier. But the next low pressure moving into California will \narrive on Sunday night and Monday. Still more low pressure systems\nmoving inland along the West Coast next week will bring \nadditional chances for precipitation, but with greater model \nspread on the track and timing.",
